## Reviewer points not followed

- uk-a 13 and uk-b 22. A space as the thousands separator is ordinary Ukrainian. This campaign’s checker does not parse it for `uk` (`dot` style). The dotted form was kept.
- uk-a 14 and uk-b 19. Q16–Q20 are body lines in the Korean source as well. The U+200B lines match that source. Promoting Q16 or deleting the characters fails `headings` or the ZWSP count.
- uk-a 12. "1,57 млн TWD" is ordinary Ukrainian. A test pins the bytes "TWD 1.57M". The figure was left.
- uk-a 2. The opened page is article 3, and the label already says so. The Korean link label still counts a 10 ("영업세법 제10조"). Dropping that 10 fails `numbers`. The parenthetical stays.
- uk-a 27. "тобто 2020" would add a Gregorian year the checker counts, and ACCEPTED-ROUND skips that. The docket number now leads, and the year is named as the Republic of China calendar, without a new digit.
- uk-b 9. "не вище розміру фактичної шкоди" alone drops the 1 in Korean "1배". The cap is "до 1 разу", parallel to "до 5 разів" and "до 3 разів".
- uk-b 17. The suggested "тобто 2020" was already in the sentence. It was kept while the docket number was moved forward. No second 2020 was added.
- uk-b 18. The English source splits the same points across lines. Merging them changes the block count. Each line was made to stand as its own sentence instead.

Nothing else in the two verdicts looked factually wrong. The case in 010 is about a Korean student; that fact was not generalized. "Найкращі інтереси дитини" is the statutory test and was left. "Кадрові" as staffing (008 "кадровому коригуванні", 018 "кадрові питання") is not the person the reviewer called "кадр".

